    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling matchups of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.18) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.01). Both players benefit from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms with xERAs above 4.30, and while their lineups remain pending, their projected spots in the three-hole provide the necessary volume to capitalize on these exploitable conditions. Meanwhile, the trio of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Gunnar Henderson** faces a significant park factor boost, as they take on Tolle. Despite a negative SP skill adjustment, the hitter-friendly venue elevates **Luis Robert Jr.** to a strong 66.52, making him an essential piece of our offensive stack. **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** also present high-value upside against Bailey Ober, leveraging strong SP skill indicators and top-of-the-order positioning to deliver efficient scores above 62.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Henry Bolte**, who sits on the bench with a 43.75 score. While **Henry Bolte** benefits from a lead-off spot projection, his matchup against the superior arm of Bryan Woo creates a volatility risk that the optimizer avoided in favor of the more stable high-floor profiles in our active OF slots. We are monitoring the status of all \"Lineup Pending\" designations closely, as any deviation from the assumed batting order could necessitate a quick pivot to protect our daily efficiency targets. Particular attention must be paid to our speed-dependent threats like **Nasim Nunez** and **Jackson Merrill**; although their raw scores hover in the 53\u201355 range, their ability to exploit opposing pitchers with slow deliveries remains our primary mechanism for maintaining an edge in the stolen base category. Proceed with caution against elite pitch-sequencing; the risk profile of these plays remains elevated until official lineups confirm their roles.",
